".any"},{"text":" match a grapheme cluster when possible,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponding with the default string representation. In addition,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matching with grapheme cluster semantics compares characters using their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"canonical representation, corresponding with how strings comparison works.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When matching with Unicode scalar semantics, metacharacters and character","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"classes always match a single Unicode scalar value, even if that scalar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comprises part of a grapheme cluster.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These semantic levels can lead to different results, especially when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"working with strings that have decomposed characters. In the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"queRegex"},{"text":" matches any 3-character string that begins with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"q\""},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let composed = \"qué\"","let decomposed = \"que\\u{301}\"","","let queRegex = \/^q..$\/","","print(composed.contains(queRegex))","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","print(decomposed.contains(queRegex))","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When using Unicode scalar semantics, however, the regular expression only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches the composed version of the string, because each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"text":" matches a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single Unicode scalar value.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code"